#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tools/c8-clientsystems-gate -- lane `c8-clientsystems`' THREE UNMEASURED CLAUSES.

    DEBUG_API_PID=<pid> tools/c8-clientsystems-gate        drive a game that is up

It ATTACHES and never launches: `tools/live-gate --keep` leaves one running, and
one process driven by several gates in turn is also one Steam authentication
rather than four. `tools/debug-api list` names the pid.

WHY THIS TOOL EXISTS. Lane `c8-clientsystems` measured its roster ordering and
the full live gate and passed both, and then could not measure three of its own
clauses because all three need a JOINED PLAYER and the box would not give it
one (status/c8-clientsystems.md, "THE THREE LANE-SPECIFIC BEHAVIOURS --
UNMEASURED, AND WHY"). Its harness lived in that session's scratchpad, which is
gone. The three clauses are:

    1. ragdolls retire under the LRU past its cap
    2. a frozen prop unfreezes
    3. the spatial partition still answers a trace AFTER a reload

EXIT CODES, the wave's convention:

    0   every clause passed
    1   a clause FAILED -- a real red, about the code
    2   NOT MEASURABLE -- a discarded trial, not a red

ASSERT POSITIVELY, NEVER FROM AN ABSENCE. `phys-wakesleep-gate` is the model
and its three guards are carried here:

  * THE CLIENT JOINED, asked of the CLIENT. `debug-api ents ss_player` is the
    SERVER's list and it answers perfectly well about a game no client ever
    reached; the reading used instead is the interpolation pass's SAMPLE count
    (`cs_cl_interp`), which runs at NetUpdatePostDataUpdateEnd and is therefore
    zero on a client that never received a net update. RenderPass must NOT be
    used: it runs at RenderStart whether or not a server was ever reached.
  * A FREE-WALK CONTROL. The player walks in the open and must cover real
    ground. A client that never joined, or a frozen player, covers nothing --
    and that makes the run VOID rather than green.
  * THE SUBJECT EXISTS AND IS IN THE STATE CLAIMED, every time, before the
    thing being tested is done to it. A prop that never spawned cannot fail to
    fall, and a gate that reads that as a pass is worse than one that reds.

AND EVERY READING IS A DISTANCE OR A POSITION, never a counter. `8f-movetypes`
had a broken roaming observer whose loop counter grew exactly like a working
build's.

WHICH LRU IS ACTUALLY UNDER TEST -- read this before believing clause 1.

The brief's wording is "ragdolls retire under the LRU past its cap", and the
LRU lane 3's table row 36 names is `CRagdollLRURetirement` in
`game/shared/ragdoll_shared.cpp`. On this tip that list has no feeder the port
can reach: its only callers are `game/server/physics_prop_ragdoll.cpp` and
`game/client/c_baseanimating.cpp` (grep, whole tree), and the port's own
corpses are managed -- `SourceSharp.Server/Corpses.cs` keeps them, with its own
cap `Limit` and stock's own retirement rule in
`RagdollRetirementPolicy.Retire`. The native rule header that said the same
thing -- "it never crashed only because nothing puts a ragdoll in the server
LRU any more" -- was deleted by lane 3f along with its gtest, because the arm
it was extracted from is an empty #else and nothing called it.

So clause 1 is measured against THE LRU THAT RUNS. Measuring the native one
would be measuring an empty list, which passes forever and says nothing -- and
a vacuously-green gate is worse than a red one.
"""
